Good morning,

We are instructed to notify a theft from the Rivergate Commons Phase II works. Our reference is AV/BR/2025/3358.

The superintendent submitted this through your portal on Sunday evening and left the policy number blank. He told us on the callback that the job has a builder's risk and that his own company has a liability policy through us as well, and he did not know which one a theft goes on. It is the builder's risk - see below.

Broker reference: AV/BR/2025/3358
Project name: Rivergate Commons Phase II
Contract number: AIA-A102-2025-RGC2
Insured name: Rivergate Development Partners, LLC
Contractor: Vanterra Construction Group, LLC
Date of loss: 17 January 2026
Loss location: 2650 Rivergate Parkway, Charlotte, NC 28273
Estimated loss: USD 394,400

They cut the fence on the Parkway frontage over the weekend, killed two cameras
and went box to box on two floors taking copper out of the conduit. They also
took unpulled reels, copper tube, plumbing trim and eight panelboards.

Everything taken is material staged for installation into the building, and the
collateral damage is to the partially completed works themselves. That is
first-party loss to insured project property. There is no third-party injury and
no damage to anyone else's property, so the contractor's liability policy does not
respond - and in any event its other insurance condition makes it excess over any
builder's risk covering the same loss.

The electrical subcontractor is missing two cordless kits from their own gang box.
That is their property and their cover, and it is not part of this claim.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * site security and loss report
  * schedule of theft and damage

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster. We would also like your position
early on the copper theft sublimit, which we expect to be the binding constraint.

